  "worked_solution": "Let $P$ be the matrix that represents the shear, and let $Q$ be the matrix that represents the scaling. These are given by the following elementary transformation matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ Q & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combined transformation can be represented by the matrix $QP:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =QP \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
